{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule targets the exact log and parses as a one-day rotation policy. The enabled, active daily logrotate timer had its next execution scheduled, a forced run successfully rotated the target, and the rule and timer persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7bc1fd1193834173","cmd-3449c22d4be84079","cmd-c5d0de4214b5432b","cmd-7d3d6a8cfe9d4169","cmd-3caacfeef7944585"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The configured policy specifies seven compressed rotations. A controlled exercise produced exactly app.log.1.gz through app.log.7.gz, all passed gzip validation, no eighth archive existed, and the count and checksums remained intact after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7bc1fd1193834173","cmd-e1697d64da034a2a","cmd-7d3d6a8cfe9d4169","cmd-3caacfeef7944585"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A descriptor opened before rotation successfully wrote afterward. The active log retained its inode, the pre-rotation marker appeared in the compressed archive, and the post-rotation marker appeared in the active log. Post-restart writing also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c5d0de4214b5432b","cmd-3caacfeef7944585"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the rule was required; forced rotations and marker appends were bounded functional and retention verification; the reboot served the mandatory restart protocol; and the temporary checksum manifest was removed. The two nonzero commands were read-only polls interrupted by the reboot. Final observations show no failed services, healthy package state, and unchanged listening endpoints apart from expected process-ID changes after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7bc1fd1193834173","cmd-c5d0de4214b5432b","cmd-e1697d64da034a2a","cmd-7d3d6a8cfe9d4169","cmd-157a94f2b8904ffc","cmd-3caacfeef7944585","cmd-b8293d9b4bd8455a","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All three public task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory restart protocol is also complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, a different boot identity appeared, and system, timer, configuration, archive, data, and write health recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The evidence window did not include a naturally triggered midnight rotation; daily cadence is demonstrated by the parsed one-day rule, active daily timer, and forced functional rotation.","No inventory application process was present during discovery; write continuity was therefore tested with an equivalent descriptor held open across rotation."]}
